  "paper_id": "asplos-2026-borrowing-dirty-qubits-in-quantum-programs-0580053e",
  "title": "Borrowing Dirty Qubits in Quantum Programs",
  "abstract": "Dirty qubits are ancillary qubits that can be borrowed from idle parts of a computation, enabling qubit reuse and reducing the demand for fresh, clean qubits---a resource that is typically scarce in practice. For such reuse to be valid, the initial states of the dirty qubits must not affect the functionality of the quantum circuits in which they are employed. Moreover, their original states, including any entanglement they possess, must be fully restored after use---a requirement commonly known as safe uncomputation.",
